    "discipline": "Mechanical",
    "subject": "Measurements, Instrumentation and Controls",
    "chapter": "Sensors and Transducers",
    "topic": "Thermistors",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Thermistors are temperature-sensitive resistors made of semiconductor materials. Two main types: NTC (Negative Temperature Coefficient) and PTC (Positive Temperature Coefficient). NTC thermistors exhibit a decrease in resistance with an increase in temperature, while PTC thermistors show the opposite behavior.</p>\r\nThe thermistor resistance is:\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$R_T=  R_0 e^{\\beta\\left(\\dfrac{1}{T} - \\dfrac{1}{T_0}\\right)}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 221</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\nwhere,\r\n$\\beta$ = material dependent value<br/>\r\nT = Temperature in Kelvin<br/>\r\n<br/>\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>The Steinhart-Hart Equation:</b></span></h5>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\dfrac{1}{T} = A + B \\ln R + C (\\ln R)^3$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 221</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\nwhere A, B and C are constants.",
    "important": "",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CIkc71fSmYpK7XBYe7kcbj1452Ouvmnf/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
